    title: "Koa’s Mobile Bar – Frequently Asked Questions",
    excerpt: "Planning a wedding or special event comes with a lot of moving pieces—and bar service is one detail couples often have questions about before reaching out. Koa’s Mobile Bar is designed to make that part easy, elevated, and stress-free. Below you’ll find answers to the most common questions we receive from couples and hosts, along with a few things people are often wondering but aren’t sure to ask. If you’re exploring whether a mobile bar is the right fit for your celebration, this FAQ will help",
    body: "Shaun Sibel\nFeb 3\n4 min read\nPlanning a wedding or special event comes with a lot of moving pieces—and bar service is one detail couples often have questions about before reaching out. Koa’s Mobile Bar is designed to make that part easy, elevated, and stress-free. Below you’ll find answers to the most common questions we receive from couples and hosts, along with a few things people are often wondering but aren’t sure to ask. If you’re exploring whether a mobile bar is the right fit for your celebration, this FAQ will help you decide with clarity and confidence.\n1.\nWhat exactly is Koa’s Mobile Bar?\nKoa’s Mobile Bar is a professionally staffed, beautifully styled bar service that comes to your wedding or event. We handle the bar setup, licensed bartenders, service flow, and guest experience—so you don’t have to worry about logistics, lines, or awkward self-serve situations.\n2.\nWhat types of events is the mobile bar best for?\nOur mobile bar is ideal for weddings, micro-weddings, elopements, rehearsal dinners, welcome parties, birthday celebrations, corporate events, and private gatherings. It works especially well for outdoor, backyard, and non-traditional venues where a permanent bar doesn’t exist.\n3.\nHow many guests can your mobile bar serve?\nWe design bar service around your guest count. Whether you’re hosting an intimate 25-person micro-wedding or a 100+ guest celebration, we’ll recommend the right number of bartenders and service style\nto keep lines short and drinks flowing smoothly.\n4.\nDo you provide the alcohol?\nTypically, clients provide the alcohol, which helps you control brands and budget. We guide you through exactly what and how much to purchase based on your guest count, event length, and drink menu. In some cases, we can assist with coordination depending on your needs.\n5.\nCan you help us decide what drinks to serve?\nAbsolutely. We help couples curate a drink menu that fits their vibe—signature cocktails, beer and wine, mocktails, or a full bar. If you’re unsure what makes sense for your crowd, we’ll walk you through popular options and what tends to work best.\n6.\nDo you offer signature cocktails or custom drink menus?\nYes. Signature cocktails are one of our most popular options. We can help you choose drinks that reflect your personalities, wedding theme, or even local flavors. Custom signage and thoughtful presentation can also be incorporated.\n7.\nWhat types of bar service do you offer?\nWe offer several service styles, including:\nBeer & wine service\nSignature cocktail service\nFull bar service\nMocktail-only or sober-friendly bar setups\nWe’ll recommend the best option based on your event size, timeline, and budget.\n8.\nAre your bartenders licensed and insured?\nYes. Our bartenders are experienced professionals, and we carry the appropriate insurance required for event bar service. We can also coordinate with your venue regarding any specific requirements.\n9.\nDo you handle setup and breakdown?\nYes. We arrive early to set up the bar, organize glassware, chill beverages, and prepare the service area. After the event, we handle breakdown so you’re not left managing cleanup at the end of the night.\n10.\nHow much space does the mobile bar need?\nOur mobile bar has a relatively small footprint, making it perfect for outdoor venues, private properties, and intimate settings. We’ll confirm space requirements ahead of time to ensure a smooth setup.\n11.\nCan the bar be set up outdoors?\nYes—outdoor events are one of our specialties. We’ll help plan for shade, weather considerations, and placement so your bar feels intentional, not improvised.\n12.\nWhat happens if it rains or the weather changes?\nWe plan for real-life conditions. If weather is a concern, we’ll work with you and your venue to identify backup locations or adjustments so bar service can continue without stress.\n13.\nDo you provide glassware, ice, and bar tools?\nYes. We provide the essential bar tools and service equipment. Glassware and ice options can be discussed based on your package and venue logistics, and we’ll make sure nothing important is overlooked.\n14.\nHow long is bar service included?\nBar service length is customizable. Most weddings choose 3–5 hours of service, but we’ll help you decide what makes sense based on your timeline, ceremony start, and reception flow.\n15.\nCan you accommodate non-drinkers or sober guests?\nDefinitely. Mocktails, non-alcoholic beers, sparkling waters, and thoughtful zero-proof options are increasingly popular—and we’re happy to make them feel just as special as alcoholic drinks.\n16.\nWill there be long lines at the bar?\nOur goal is efficient, professional service. We recommend staffing and menu choices that minimize wait times, especially during high-demand moments like cocktail hour.\n17.\nDo you work with our venue and planner?\nYes. We coordinate directly with your venue, planner, or coordinator to align on timing, rules, and layout. This helps your event run smoothly behind the scenes.\n18.\nIs the mobile bar a good fit for small or micro-weddings?\nAbsolutely. In fact, smaller weddings are where a mobile bar really shines—it adds polish and experience without feeling over-the-top or impersonal.\n19.\nHow far in advance should we book the mobile bar?\nPopular dates book quickly, especially during wedding season. We recommend reaching out as soon as you have your date and venue secured to ensure availability.\n20.\nHow do we get pricing and check availability?\nThe best next step is to contact us directly. We’ll confirm availability for your date, walk you through package options, and help you decide if Koa’s Mobile Bar is the right fit for your event.\nIf Koa’s Mobile Bar sounds like the right fit for your wedding or event, we’d love to hear more about what you’re planning. Reach out to check availability, explore bar service options, and get a personalized quote based on your guest count, location, and vision. Whether you’re still in the early planning stages or finalizing details, we’re here to help make your celebration feel effortless and well cared for.\nReady to get started?\nContact us to see if your date is available and start planning your bar experience.",
